# Octop CONTRIBUTING alignment

Before committing or opening a PR in this repo, follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md):

## Branch / PR target

- Feature work: branch from **`develop`**, open PR **into `develop`** (not `main`).
- Never bulk-merge `develop` → `main`; releases go `release/x.y.z` → `main`.

## Quality gate

- Keep `make install-hooks` enabled; **do not skip pre-commit** (`--no-verify`) unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Pre-commit runs **`make all`** (+ dashboard build). Wait for it; do not treat a long test run as stuck without checking progress.
- Prefer `make check-all` when both backend and frontend changed.
- Add/update tests for behavior changes; keep cross-platform rules in AGENTS.md §7.

## User-facing changes

- Update **`CHANGELOG.md`** under `[Unreleased]` when behavior is user-visible.

## PR description (CONTRIBUTING checklist)

Include:

- [ ] UI screenshots / feature demo (upload on the GitHub PR itself — **not** a docs/image-hosting branch)
- [ ] Tests added and passing
- [ ] CI expected green
- [ ] Minimal-change / one problem per PR
- [ ] Clear test plan

For UI screenshots: redact privacy (usernames, home paths, emails, credentials) before upload.
